      "source": [
        "# 5. Data Preparation\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Dataset Information:\")\n",
        "df.info()\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nMissing Values:\")\n",
        "print(df.isnull().sum())\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nDuplicate Records:\")\n",
        "print(df.duplicated().sum())\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nExperimental Groups:\")\n",
        "print(df[\"group\"].value_counts())\n"
      ],
        "To build valid causal uplift models, we must follow these guidelines strictly:\n",
        "- **No Post-Treatment Leakage**: Variables like `redeem`, `amount`, and `discount` are determined *after* the treatment is administered. Using them to predict uplift would corrupt our model with post-treatment bias.\n",
        "- **No Identifier Bias**: We exclude `consumer_id`.\n",
        "- **Pre-treatment Predictors**: We use `pageviews` and `visit` as baseline consumer activity features ($X$).\n",
        "- **Target variable**: `purchase` ($y$).\n",
        "\n",
        "We will segment our data into two sub-experiments to keep the comparison clean:\n",
        "1. **Low-Tier Sub-experiment**: `CGL` vs `T1L`\n",
        "2. **High-Tier Sub-experiment**: `CGH` vs `T1H` (and optionally `T2H` separately, or as distinct treatment levels)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "W5E6T4t1Z2vz",
        "outputId": "d1504cc9-550f-4937-eefb-c29ec215966b"
      },
      "execution_count": 7,
        "id": "2992889f",
        "outputId": "11963551-0226-4a17-846e-cf9e926f27ce"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Define Low-Tier Dataset\n",
        "df_low = df[df['group'].isin(['CGL', 'T1L'])].copy()\n",
        "df_low['treatment'] = np.where(df_low['group'] == 'T1L', 1, 0)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Define High-Tier Dataset (comparing CGH with both T1H and T2H)\n",
        "df_high = df[df['group'].isin(['CGH', 'T1H', 'T2H'])].copy()\n",
        "df_high['treatment'] = np.where(df_high['group'] != 'CGH', 1, 0)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Let's inspect shapes and ensure the splits are correct\n",
        "print(f\"Low-Tier experiment shape: {df_low.shape} (CGL vs T1L)\")\n",
        "print(f\"High-Tier experiment shape: {df_high.shape} (CGH vs T1H, T2H)\")\n",
        "print(\"\\nFeatures used for training: ['pageviews', 'visit']\")"
      ],
      "execution_count": 14,
