            "T1H                 37.693  \n",
            "T1L                 27.821  \n",
            "T2H                 31.899  \n"
          ]
        }
        "Uplift modelling predicts the **incremental impact** of an action on a customer's behavior. Instead of predicting whether a customer will buy (which targets people who would have bought anyway), uplift targets those who only buy *because* of the treatment.\n",
        "\n",
        "We use a **T-Learner (Two-Model Approach)**:\n",
        "- **Control Model ($M_0$)**: Predicts $P(Y | X, W=0)$ using control customers.\n",
        "- **Treatment Model ($M_1$)**: Predicts $P(Y | X, W=1)$ using treated customers.\n",
        "- **Individual Uplift Score**: $\\tau(X) = M_1(X) - M_0(X)$"
      ]
    },
