      "source": [
        "# 7. Model Evaluation\n",
        "\n",
        "To evaluate our uplift model, we compute the **Cumulative Uplift**. We sort our test customers by their predicted uplift score in descending order. Then, we track the cumulative difference in purchase rates between the treatment and control groups as we target increasingly larger portions of the population. A successful model will show a steep curve at the beginning, indicating that we can capture most of the incremental gains by only targeting a small fraction of high-uplift customers."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cf2bfe2c"
      },
      "source": [
        "# 8. Customer Segmentation\n",
        "\n",
        "Using the predicted uplift scores, we can segment customers into actionable business cohorts:\n",
        "- **High Expected Uplift (Persuadables)**: Customers who are highly responsive to the coupon. This is the primary target group.\n",
        "- **Medium/Low Expected Uplift (Sure Things or Lost Causes)**: Customers whose purchasing probability is largely unaffected by receiving a coupon. Offering a discount here represents budget waste.\n",
        "- **Negative Expected Uplift (Do Not Disturbs / Sleeping Dogs)**: Customers who respond negatively to being targeted (e.g., unsubscribe or reduce purchase rate)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 1000
        },
        "id": "efcc8de1",
        "outputId": "66fe84c8-4da3-43d5-ac54-7e8d0282ac5b"
      },
      "source": [
        "def segment_by_uplift(test_df, label):\n",
        "    # Segment based on thresholds\n",
        "    # We define > 0.01 as High Uplift, between -0.01 and 0.01 as Neutral/Medium, and < -0.01 as Negative Uplift\n",
        "    def assign_segment(score):\n",
        "        if score > 0.01:\n",
        "            return 'High expected uplift (Persuadables)'\n",
        "        elif score < -0.01:\n",
        "            return 'Negative expected uplift (Do Not Disturb)'\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            return 'Low/Neutral expected uplift (Lost Causes / Sure Things)'\n",
        "\n",
        "    df_segmented = test_df.copy()\n",
        "    df_segmented['segment'] = df_segmented['uplift_score'].apply(assign_segment)\n",
        "\n",
        "    summary = df_segmented['segment'].value_counts(normalize=True).reset_index()\n",
        "    summary.columns = ['Segment', 'Proportion']\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(f\"--- {label} Customer Segments ---\")\n",
        "    display(summary)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Visualize the segments\n",
        "    plt.figure(figsize=(8, 4))\n",
        "    plt.barh(summary['Segment'], summary['Proportion'], color=['forestgreen', 'orange', 'crimson'])\n",
        "    plt.title(f'Customer Segments Proportion - {label}')\n",
        "    plt.xlabel('Proportion of Test Population')\n",
        "    plt.grid(axis='x', linestyle='--')\n",
        "    plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "    plt.show()\n",
        "\n",
        "    return df_segmented\n",
        "\n",
        "test_low_seg = segment_by_uplift(test_low, \"Low-Tier\")\n",
        "test_high_seg = segment_by_uplift(test_high, \"High-Tier\")"
      ],
