      "source": [
        "# 9. Budget Optimization\n",
        "\n",
        "When working in a business setting, budgets are finite. Sending coupons to every consumer is highly inefficient because it wastes money on users who would purchase anyway or who are completely unresponsive.\n",
        "\n",
        "To demonstrate the business value of uplift modeling, we will establish a budget optimization simulation comparing two approaches:\n",
        "1. **Untargeted Strategy**: Distribute coupons randomly or to all customers uniformly until the budget is depleted.\n",
        "2. **Uplift-Optimized Strategy**: Prioritize targeting customers starting from the highest predicted positive uplift score down, maximizing the yield of incremental purchases for our available budget.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Illustrative Assumptions:\n",
        "- **Low-tier coupon cost**: $1.00 per contact\n",
        "- **High-tier coupon cost**: $5.00 per contact\n",
        "- **Total illustrative budget**: $2,500.00"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "e121eb27",
        "outputId": "74b14730-c71d-489a-ba23-953e40191a75"
      },
      "source": [
        "def optimize_budget(test_df, coupon_cost, budget, label):\n",
        "    # Sort by predicted uplift score descending\n",
        "    sorted_df = test_df.sort_values(by='uplift_score', ascending=False).copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Strategy 1: Target All (Random order since we don't use model prioritization)\n",
        "    random_df = test_df.sample(frac=1, random_state=42).copy()\n",
        "    random_df['cumulative_cost'] = (np.arange(len(random_df)) + 1) * coupon_cost\n",
        "    targeted_all = random_df[random_df['cumulative_cost'] <= budget]\n",
        "    # Expected incremental purchases in targeted group = sum of individual uplift scores\n",
        "    incremental_purchases_all = targeted_all['uplift_score'].sum()\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Strategy 2: Model-Optimized Targeting\n",
        "    sorted_df['cumulative_cost'] = (np.arange(len(sorted_df)) + 1) * coupon_cost\n",
        "    targeted_opt = sorted_df[sorted_df['cumulative_cost'] <= budget]\n",
        "    incremental_purchases_opt = targeted_opt['uplift_score'].sum()\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(f\"=== Budget Optimization Results for {label} (Budget: ${budget}) ===\")\n",
        "    print(f\"Target All / Random Strategy:\")\n",
        "    print(f\"  - Customers targeted: {len(targeted_all)}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"  - Expected incremental purchases: {incremental_purchases_all:.2f}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"  - Cost per incremental purchase: ${budget / (incremental_purchases_all + 1e-9):.2f}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"\\nUplift-Optimized Strategy:\")\n",
        "    print(f\"  - Customers targeted: {len(targeted_opt)}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"  - Expected incremental purchases: {incremental_purchases_opt:.2f}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"  - Cost per incremental purchase: ${budget / (incremental_purchases_opt + 1e-9):.2f}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"  - Efficiency improvement: {((incremental_purchases_opt - incremental_purchases_all) / (incremental_purchases_all + 1e-9)) * 100:.1f}%\")\n",
        "    print(\"=\" * 60 + \"\\n\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Run the optimization simulation on our test partitions\n",
        "optimize_budget(test_low_seg, coupon_cost=1.00, budget=1000.00, label=\"Low-Tier\")\n",
        "optimize_budget(test_high_seg, coupon_cost=5.00, budget=1500.00, label=\"High-Tier\")"
      ],
      "execution_count": 18,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
