      "source": [
        "# 11. Business Recommendations\n",
        "\n",
        "Based on our Uplift Modeling and Budget Optimization, here are our strategic recommendations:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Implement Uplift-based Targeting immediately**:\n",
        "   - In the Low-Tier group, optimizing coupon allocation can double (+104.7%) the number of incremental purchases achieved for the exact same budget.\n",
        "   - In the High-Tier group, the gains are even more extreme. Instead of wasting expensive coupons ($5.00 each) randomly, targeting only 'Persuadables' improves efficiency by **528.8%** and avoids wasting budget on people who purchase anyway.\n",
        "\n",
        "2. **De-escalate Unnecessary Discounts (Avoid the \"Sure Things\")**:\n",
        "   - Over 60% of both populations fall into the 'Low/Neutral Uplift' segment. Many of these consumers are 'Sure Things' who buy regardless of getting a coupon. Suppressing coupons for this group directly preserves profit margins without hurting sales.\n",
        "\n",
        "3. **Monitor \"Do Not Disturb\" Segments**:\n",
        "   - In the High-Tier campaign, we detected about 6.3% of users who have a negative response to the aggressive coupon offerings. For these users, coupon communication might feel like spam, or trigger negative brand associations, leading to lower purchase rates. We must actively exclude these users from high-intensity campaigns."
      ]
    },
