        "# 12. Limitations and Conclusion\n",
        "\n",
        "### Limitations\n",
        "1. **Feature Constraints**: Our model relied exclusively on basic navigation actions (`pageviews` and `visit`). Adding richer demographic features or historic transaction history could significantly improve the precision of the uplift predictions.\n",
        "2. **Short-Term Scope**: The experiment evaluates short-term conversions. We cannot observe long-term lifetime value changes or customer fatigue from continuous coupon usage.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Conclusion\n",
        "Uplift modeling with a T-Learner approach successfully separated organic buyers from treatment-sensitive buyers. Rather than predicting purchase likelihood, focusing on **incremental impact** allows the business to slash budget waste, maximize conversion gains, and establish highly efficient pricing and incentive structures."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Customer segmentation based on predicted uplift\n",
        "\n",
        "def segment_customers(data, name):\n",
        "\n",
        "    data = data.copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "    data['customer_segment'] = pd.cut(\n",
        "        data['uplift_score'],\n",
        "        bins=[-np.inf, 0, 0.02, np.inf],\n",
        "        labels=[\n",
        "            'Negative Uplift',\n",
        "            'Low/Moderate Uplift',\n",
        "            'High Uplift'\n",
        "        ]\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(f\"\\n{name} - Customer Segments\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    summary = data.groupby(\n",
        "        'customer_segment',\n",
        "        observed=False\n",
        "    ).agg(\n",
        "        customer_count=('consumer_id', 'count'),\n",
        "        average_uplift=('uplift_score', 'mean'),\n",
        "        actual_purchase_rate=('purchase', 'mean')\n",
        "    ).reset_index()\n",
        "\n",
        "    display(summary)\n",
        "\n",
        "    return data, summary\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# Segment all three comparisons\n",
        "\n",
        "test_low, segment_low = segment_customers(\n",
        "    test_low, \"Low-tier\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "test_high_t1, segment_high_t1 = segment_customers(\n",
        "    test_high_t1, \"High-tier T1\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "test_high_t2, segment_high_t2 = segment_customers(\n",
        "    test_high_t2, \"High-tier T2\"\n",
        ")"
      ],
